  - wide-trail-strategy
abstract: >-
  RSD-S (Riemann Spectral Diffusion) is an experimental keyed 512-bit SPN
  diffusion and hashing research prototype operating over pairs of elements in
  F_p (p = 2^255 - 19). It documents the complete empirical and algebraic
  evolution from v0 (linear transformation) through v4 (16x16-bit full
  fragmentation per input, GF(2^16) inversion S-box with proven differential
  uniformity 4, and 32x32 Cauchy MDS diffusion with branch number 33),
  accompanied by Z3 SMT proofs, synthesized XOR/DIMACS CNF circuits, and
  multi-round concrete differential trail searches.
